To create a reportwriter database follow the steps below. For this
example assume the database name is "reportwriter".


1) Create new database (using port forwarding to rarely used port 3312)

   docker run --name mysql-container \
   -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=$RW_API_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD \
   -e MYSQL_DATABASE=reportwriter \
   -p 3312:3306 \
   -d mysql:8.4

2) Use mysql to load the data.

   docker exec -i mysql-container mysql -u$RW_API_DATASOURCE_USERNAME -p$RW_API_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD reportwriter < /path/to/your/init.sql

3) Make a test query to the new database.

   docker exec -it mysql-container mysql -u$RW_API_DATASOURCE_USERNAME -p$RW_API_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD -D reportwriter -e "SELECT * FROM lk_source LIMIT 10;"


